                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1134-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Shure Beta 98A</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Beta 98A is a revision of the company&#8217;s Beta 98, also a miniature cardioid condenser microphone intended for instrumental miking applications. The mic was introduced at the AES show in late 2010, as part of a revamp of the entire Beta product line.</p><p>Like the original, the Beta 98A has a two-piece design. The capsule head is small, which allows easier positioning in a studio context as well as making the microphone less visible on stage. The microphone&#8217;s amplifier circuitry is housed separately, and can be located up to 25 feet from the capsule head.</p><p>The &#8220;A&#8221; revision of the Beta 98 incorporates a new electret capsule design, which brings higher sensitivity and lower self-noise:</p><table><tr><td></td><td><b>Sensitivity</b></td><td><b>Self-Noise</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>Beta 98</b></td><td>1 mV/Pa</td><td>35 dBA</td></tr><tr><td><b>Beta 98A</b></td><td>4 mV/Pa</td><td>30 dBA</td></tr></table><p>The 98A revision does not incorporate a new amplifier circuit. The included inline preamplifier for the 98A is identical to the one used for the Beta 98. Both connect to their respective capsule heads via Shure&#8217;s &#8220;TQG&#8221; cable (included with the mic).</p><p>Note that the Beta 98AMP&#8217;s integrated preamplifier differs in sound and specifications from the Beta 98 / Beta 98A inline preamplifier. The original Beta 98 preamp design was revised and improved during the 98AMP design process.</p><blockquote><p><cite>John Born, Shure</cite></p><p>The only difference between the Beta 98A/C and Beta 98AD/C is the included hardware. The AD/C versions come with the drum mount, [whereas] the /C version comes with a swivel mic stand mount. Both include the external preamp and new capsule design.</p></blockquote><p>The mic includes a zippered pouch (Shure p/n 95A2314), an in-line preamplifier (p/n RPM626), and a snap-on windscreen (p/n 95A2064). Included mounting hardware varies by model:</p><table><tr><td></td><td><b>Includes</b></td></tr><tr><td><b>Beta 98A/C</b></td><td>Shock-mount swivel adapter (p/n RK282)</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Lightweight 25ft cable (p/n 95A2398)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Beta 98AD/C</b></td><td>Drum mount (p/n A98D)</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Heavy-duty 15ft cable (p/n C98D)</td></tr></table><p><p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Shure/Beta-98A">Shure Beta-98A</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2010.</p>
